  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The relation between two temperature scales can be written as follows</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>65</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>65</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>212</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mn>180</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters in to equation (1) and sole to calculate the required temperature in Fahrenheit scale.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>65</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>95</mn></mrow><mn>80</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>212</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mn>180</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>212</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>F</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>212</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>360</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>148</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>",
